---
description: Route Go tasks through the installed golang-skills pack
alwaysApply: true
---

For Go work, use the skills from this plugin before the first edit:

1. Load `go-code` to write or fix Go, `go-code-refactor` for a refactor that
   preserves behavior, or `go-code-review` for a review.
2. For writing, fixing, or refactoring, also load `go-style-core` in full;
   it includes the current Go idiom card.
3. Load only the owner skills named by the router for this task.

Use the installed skill entries to find their directories. Read each selected
`SKILL.md` whole, using the plugin-qualified name when the host provides one.
Name the skills loaded before the first edit. No hook enforces these loads in
Cursor. If the task is not Go work, ignore this rule.
